Hello hello.

Wolfe here. Having taken a long hiatus from nethack (after MrMorden
the invulnerable mage and Torquemada the weaponless-almost-vegetarian
Monk made it to the Demibar), I've had the bug bit me again, due to
two things:

- The story of Ellora, the unspoiled elven archer. Man, what a
fantastic read it has been; I've read the >400page thing like three
times already. Inspiring.
- The discovery of neoGNUd ( http://www.linuxgames.co.za/noeGNUd/ ) ,
a really kick-ass piece of frontend that is mouth-watering to look at,
has hundreds of options, supports vanilla & Slash'EM and works like a
charm.

So, my heart rekindled, and noticing that I've never ascended in
Slash'EM, I decided to give Boogie the Mafia Hit-man (Rogue with
firearms) a chance to clean up all these vecna, sam and ruggo weird
people who supposedly dwell there. He's ATM still mopping up between
the mines and sokoban.

Now, my questions:
A) I have, say, 50 scrolls in a chest. I want to take three of these.
#loot, yes, 3a, enter. You get 50 scrolls, you are now strained. Same
happens when putting things in, or when applying a bag. Long story
short, I've tried all combinations and permutations of menu_style,
loot_abc and other seemingly applicable options, but I can't just get
three scrolls from the bag/chest.

I read somewhere that with the mouse you could twiddle with a knob,
but I can't make it work in neoGNUd (maybe noeGNUD-specific bug?), and
it's not quite acceptable - I like using keyboard only. This used to
work in older nethacks, and it's frustrating me no end. Ideas,
pointers and options are very welcome.

B) When I kill a monster and it leaves a corpse, the interface to eat
it is different than I was used to. Instead of "there's a foo corpse
here, eat it? (y/n)", I get "what do you want to eat? [xyz ?*,]", with
the new "," option being the corpse on the floor (sort of makes sense,
pick-up-and-eat); hitting "," then opens a little pop-up window with
the list of things on the floor. Select the one you want and it's
eaten - easy, no? but two problems:

B-1) The letters it chooses for the things on the floor are not
consistently "a, b, c, d", but rather seem to be from the name of the
thing: "h - a hobbit corpse, w - a white unicorn corpse". This is
REALLY annoying! Now eating from the floor is not an automatic "e y"
or "e , a", but "e , <look at screen> <look at keyboard> <hit
letter>". Really breaks my finger-memory. Is this controlled by an
option, or compile-time choice or something else? Is this
neoGNUd-specific? I need consistency!

B-2) Looking for a consistent solution for B-1, I tried "e , .",
assuming it would select all items on the floor (just the one corpse)
and let me eat it without looking at the keyboard. No dice, "."
doesn't select it. In fact, all key combinations I tried were
uneffective. Other than the right letter or clicking on the thing, I
can't just say "eat the thing on the floor, whatever the hell it is!".
Tried . + * @ and a couple of others, the damed corpse wouldn't be
selected. Frustrating.


As said before, I'm playing slashem-0.0.7E3 with neoGNUd-0.8.0 as
front end, on Linux (Mandrake 10), 3d-tiled mode with the absurd set
(sooooo sexy). I don't know if either of these are specific to
variant, frontend or OS. I would really appreciate any ideas or
pointers to make the game flow better for me.


